<title>INDIA: Indian Shipping -- Mangalore cargoes - Nov 27.</title>
<headline>Indian Shipping -- Mangalore cargoes - Nov 27.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the berthing schedule</p>
<p>of major vessels loading and unloading at India's Mangalore port</p>
<p>on November 27:</p>
<p>  Commodity	     Tons		   Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>		    (LDD/ULD) (Balance)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Scrap		   743 (ULD)  3,242    Beta Luck	  7/11</p>
<p> Timber		  130 (ULD)  4,243    Vanda Naree     24/11</p>
<p> P.Acid		9,500 (ULD)    ---    Bow Heron	 27/11</p>
<p> Granite		 383 (LDD)  2,152    C.Clipper	 23/11</p>
<p> Granite	     2,110 (LDD)  1,890    Sakala	    25/11</p>
<p>Iron Ore</p>
<p>  Concentrate	7,000 (LDD) 53,000    Panamax Pearl   26/11</p>
<p> LPG		   3,500 (ULD)    ---    Nanga Parbat    26/11</p>
<p> Crude		90,000 (ULD)    ---    Jag Ladki	 27/11</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Note:</p>
<p>ULD-Discharge</p>
<p>LDD-Loading</p>
<p>(Source: J.M.Baxi &amp; Co, Mangalore)</p>
